  "title": "Bound supplier purchase-invoice scalar money and registration arithmetic",
  "description": "Close procurement payable invoice write/freeze numeric gaps. PurchaseInvoiceRules.ValidateAmounts currency-rounds three unlimited decimals then directly computes net+tax and error differences; it never checks the actual configured decimal(18,2) columns. Huge individually positive inputs can overflow CLR arithmetic or fail SQL despite a valid amount equation. NormalizeAllocationAmount similarly only checks positive. Bound each scalar after existing currency rounding before equation or persistence; keep zero-tax and zero-net invoices supported where existing rules permit. Revalidate stored invoice fields at RecordAsync inside existing deterministic source/invoice locks; refuse inconsistent stored currency amounts instead of repairing snapshots. Do not limit read-side aggregates. Reuse existing scalar FinancePersistedAmountRules where actual columns match; never cap global CurrencyAmountRules.RoundAmount, historical read-only aggregate totals or legitimate multi-document sums. Preserve supported currencies, AwayFromZero rounding, nullable source semantics, existing ownership/menu/customer authority and source locks. Do not require unrelated master-maintenance grants. No schema/migration changes or production access. Preserve historical reads and void/cancel/reversal semantics without new draft validation gates. Adapt all necessary original unit/SQL fixtures with genuine live identities/masters, preserving original assertions. Full original failure logs retained; explicit logs/TRX/results under .ai/logs/<task> only. Retain existing live identity/menu/customer-scope authority, transactions, source locks, controlled errors and audit. Reject before numbering or persistence, with zero header/detail/source/status mutations. No new permissions, schema, production access, external service or arbitrary SQL. Genuine SQL only on (localdb)\\NEWERP_AutoAcceptance with Integrated Security and a fresh GUID-owned NEWERP_AUTOTEST database; reject wrong/existing targets and never drop/reset. Require safe Release with analyzers/warnings-as-errors, full units and relevant genuine SQL/browser tests; accurately record blockers and do not claim whole-stage acceptance.",
